Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,You wake in the night\Nbecause something
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.50,0:00:04.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,near your bed made a\Nsound.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.68,0:00:07.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,You open your eyes,\Nand the black
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.23,0:00:09.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,above you is not the\Nceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.78,0:00:13.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,It is two empty holes\Nwhere eyes should be.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.38,0:00:16.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,Something dark is\Nrunning out of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.28,0:00:18.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,Let us go back to the\Nbeginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.49,0:00:20.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,Mitch lost his house\Nthat spring,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.99,0:00:23.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,so his brother Edwin\Ntook him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.94,0:00:27.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,A cheap house at the\Nend of a long street,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.15,0:00:29.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,pine woods behind the\Nfence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.59,0:00:31.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,He took the back room.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.32,0:00:34.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,A week in, a rustling\Nunder his window
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.49,0:00:37.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,woke him at one in the\Nmorning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.38,0:00:39.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,Probably a raccoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.31,0:00:42.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,The next night he woke\Nall at once, sure
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.56,0:00:45.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,he had heard the\Nwindow lifted open.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.94,0:00:49.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then a soft, heavy\Nthump, like a person
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.11,0:00:51.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,landing with their\Nknees bent.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.86,0:00:53.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,The window was shut.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.58,0:00:55.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the morning Edwin\Ndropped
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.59,0:00:56.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,his coffee cup.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.97,0:00:59.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,There was a long clean\Ncut down Mitch's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.80,0:01:02.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,cheek, and he had not\Nfelt it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.43,0:01:05.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,The doctor said it was\Nprobably sleepwalking.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.43,0:01:08.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then he asked him to\Nlift his shirt.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.37,0:01:11.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,There was a surgical\Ncut in his side,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.35,0:01:13.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,closed with neat\Nstitches.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.74,0:01:16.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,His left kidney was\Ngone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.04,0:01:19.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,That evening he went\Nback to the same room.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.39,0:01:21.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,At midnight he opened\Nhis eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.96,0:01:24.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,and it stood over his\Nbed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.56,0:01:25.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,A black hood.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.76,0:01:29.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,A face the colour of\Nold grey paint,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.12,0:01:31.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,with no nose and no\Nmouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.00,0:01:34.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,His hand went sideways\Non its
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.33,0:01:36.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,own, to the camera on\Nthe shelf,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.90,0:01:39.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,and took the picture.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.04,0:01:40.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,The flash filled the\Nroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.89,0:01:42.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then the dark came\Nback,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.67,0:01:44.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,and it came at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.52,0:01:47.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,He kicked it in the\Nface, ran barefoot
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.58,0:01:51.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,into the woods, and\Ntripped on a rock.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.08,0:01:53.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,He woke in a hospital\Nbed, and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.65,0:01:56.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,the doctor sat down,\Nwhich nobody
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.47,0:01:59.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,does when the news is\Ngood.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.23,0:02:01.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,Mitch was only\Nbruised.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.12,0:02:02.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,His brother had been\Nfound
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.77,0:02:04.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,in the house that\Nmorning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.88,0:02:07.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,Three days later he\Nwent back
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.18,0:02:09.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,for his things, and\Nfrom his door
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.80,0:02:12.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,he saw down the\Nhallway.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.16,0:02:14.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Beside his brother was\Nsomething
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.70,0:02:16.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,small, wrapped in\Ncloth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.90,0:02:19.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,He carried it out to\Nthe car.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.04,0:02:21.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two streets away he\Nopened it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.67,0:02:24.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,It was the piece taken\Nout of his
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.24,0:02:27.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,side, and some of it\Nwas gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.02,0:02:30.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,The photograph is\Nstill on that camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.17,0:02:32.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,It is dark and\Nblurred, but the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.53,0:02:35.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,hood and the holes are\Nthere.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.19,0:02:36.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,And in the picture it\Nis
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.87,0:02:38.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,not looking at Mitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.64,0:02:42.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,It is looking past\Nhim, at his open door.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.21,0:02:46.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is my retelling\Nof the creepypasta
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.56,0:02:48.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,Eyeless Jack, posted
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.79,0:02:52.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,by a user called\NAzelf5000.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.26,0:02:54.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,Would you have taken\Nthe photograph?
